COSMIC Studio actual IcedElement keyboard wrapper route (iteration32)

Original panel: b5cc19e351b82eed999097ced1ff267d27bf8e7a
Original GPL sources/complete license retained in pinned-keyboard-focus-sources.json.gz
and pinned-keyboard-focus.LICENSE; original State in pinned-iced-state.json.gz.
Authored iced_keyboard_route.rs and prepare_iced_keyboard_route.py: GPL-3.0-only.
Prior authored GPL, original MPL seat and MIT/Winit forward-table notices unchanged.

Requires exact complete iteration31 corrected State dispatch postimages. Changes
only wrapper receiver type/two fresh constructor conversions, adds its child
module, and exposes the State dispatch child to its parent wrapper. Ordinary
update/filter/target/client callbacks/overflow/popup-grab paths remain unchanged.

TaskInbox stages at most the next original Option<Message> when probing pending
output. None is an output too; repeated refusal does not consume/reorder it.
Ordinary update uses the same try_recv semantics. State work refuses before the
receiver probe. This is not a scheduler barrier: an in-flight output may arrive
later and stays ordinary work, never attributed to the supplied keyboard event.

Actual wrapper explicitly calls State::update_keyboard; caller must supply live
validation and keyboard-only envelope-bearing dispatch outside Smithay locks.
Returned tasks follow original contextless scheduling. Synthetic wrapper/UI tests
use a real calloop handle but do not dispatch a live GlobalState or Wayland seat.
No native callback uses this route, no validator/grab grant is implemented, no
keyboard recovery/activation/hiding/config/deployment/runtime acceptance claimed.
